<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  网络安全配置 / network security configuration
  ============================================================================
  中文
  ====
  为什么需要它:

  PrintTheShot 的 Web UI 要访问局域网里的服务端,地址形如
  `http://192.168.1.100:8000` —— 明文 HTTP,没有证书。而 Android 从 API 28
  (Android 9) 起,App 默认**禁止**明文流量,不开这个口子的话,页面里所有
  请求都会以 `CLEARTEXT communication not permitted` 失败。

  这份配置把明文允许打开,和 AndroidManifest 里的
  `android:usesCleartextTraffic="true"` 是一致的:API 24 起以本文件为准,
  两边都写成允许,行为才不会有分歧。

  想收紧的话 / to tighten this later:
    把 base-config 改成 cleartextTrafficPermitted="false",再加一段
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true"> 只放行你的服务端地址
    (内网域名或固定 IP)。这样除该地址外一律走 HTTPS,更安全。

    Set base-config to cleartextTrafficPermitted="false" and add a
    <domain-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true"> listing just your server
    host (a LAN hostname or a fixed IP). Everything else then requires HTTPS.

  English
  =======
  The PrintTheShot web UI talks to a service on the LAN over plain HTTP, e.g.
  `http://192.168.1.100:8000`. Since Android 9 (API 28) cleartext traffic is
  blocked by default, and without this file every request from the page would
  fail with `CLEARTEXT communication not permitted`.

  This config opens that door, consistently with
  `android:usesCleartextTraffic="true"` in the manifest (from API 24 this file
  takes precedence, so both are set to allow).

  Note there is deliberately no exemption for the WebView's own origin: with
  `androidScheme: "http"` in capacitor.config.json the page itself is served
  from http://localhost, which this base-config also covers.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
